{"name":"Purple Dusk","hex":"#7c6b76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"dusk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to darkness or blackness; moderately dark or black; dusky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time after the sun has set but when the sky is still lit by sunlight; the evening twilight period.","A darkish colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusk","blocks":[{"text":"Dusk occurs at the darkest stage of twilight, or at the very end of astronomical twilight after sunset and just before nightfall. At predusk, during early to intermediate stages of twilight, enough light in the sky under clear conditions may occur to read outdoors without artificial illumination; however, at the end of civil twilight, such lighting is required to read outside. The term dusk usually refers to astronomical dusk, or the darkest part of twilight before night begins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg/330px-Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusk","wikidata":"Q11288132"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg/330px-Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg/330px-Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg/250px-Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, h